// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 19 „A2 kirjutamine ja rääkimine” (a2-091…095), level A2, in the final shape
// (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_A2.md, row m19 = m3: KUUL PROB LUGU AVAS, with the leads of modules 11–19; gates V1–V16 of
// docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B1.md §8). One storyline, November, a year before the B1 course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md). The autumn course at Keelekool Sõna (Mondays and
// Wednesdays at 18–20; Maret, Aune, administrator Ene; Sofia, Tom, Lucía, Dmitri, Olga) holds Keelekooli õhtu on Friday 19 November at 18. It is planned for Jaan's café
// Pann; a burst pipe closes Pann until 22 November, so the evening moves to the school's big room 305 and the cakes come from pagariäri Mesi (Piret). The new learner
// Natalja Orlova tells how she sat in a German lesson. Everyone speaks for two minutes on the evening. Module 19 has no art of its own: 092 uses the picture of lesson a2-028
// (Anna orders from Jaan), 095 the picture of lesson a2-068 (Sofia and Aune at the study plan).
//   091 KUUL L→W  a voice message becomes an invitation: reedel / reedeks, Kas sa saad + da-vorm, Kahjuks …, sest …; corner L2 (radio talk, true / false);
//                 main: an invitation of 40–70 words (W03).
//   092 PROB L→S  a call about what changed, a first try, language, a second try: Kas teil on kooki? Siis võtan koogi, … on otsas, hoopis; corner R1 (set phrases in short talks);
//                 S05 = `092_p_cards`; main: the problem solved by phone (S10); home recording: the picture (S06).
//   093 LUGU R→W  Natalja's first lesson, cliffhanger: the stranger's textbook; kõigepealt, siis, seepärast, lõpuks; corner W2b (a description with three prompts);
//                 main: the story goes on, 60–80 words (W05), edited (W10).
//   094 AVAS R→S  try first → the plan of a talk → try again: Ma räägin oma tööst, kõigepealt, teiseks, näiteks, kokkuvõtteks; corner R1 (phrases at the evening);
//                 main: a talk of 1.5–2 minutes with three questions after it (S02).
//   095 EKS       the module exam, every part timed (B.examPart): R1–R5, W1, W2b, L1–L4, S0, S1, S2. Reading + writing on Harjuta, listening + speaking on Kasuta.
// Every teaching lesson: „Mäletad?” naming the previous lesson and one of modules 15–17, an in-lesson pair task, a home recording in Kasuta, two fluency tasks,
// one exam corner. No tingiv kõneviis (A2): „Kas sa saad …?”, never „Kas sa saaksid …?”.
